rd status surfacing (P0)\"] --> E003[\"E003 Status documentation (P1)\"]\n    E002[\"E002 KServe condition contract validation (P1)\"] --> E003\n```\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| (root) E001 | — | Dashboard implementation is unblocked: the InferenceService status conditions and events it consumes already exist in-platform (architecture context, kserve.md); the strategy marks nothing blocking. |\n| (root) E002 | Rule 14 | Validation of an existing contract in a different repo (kserve) with no artifact produced that E001 builds against — the conditions already exist; E002 confirms them. Parallel by design; a serial edge would mis-sequence independent work. |\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by all Implementation epics — docs describe what was built. |\n| E002 → E003 | Rule 11 | Same: documentation of status values must reflect the validated condition semantics, not just the Dashboard rendering. |\n\nNo `konflux-onboarding` edges apply: Dashboard and KServe are both already\nKonflux-onboarded per architecture context, and Documentation is handled through\nthe docs content process. No conditional branches (no Investigation epics).\ndocs-authoring edges do not trigger priority inheritance (Step 4 exception);\nE003's P1 comes from the strategy frontmatter priority `Major` → P1.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 (status shown per deployed model) | P0 | E001 | |\n| HLR-2 (status detail view: conditions + events) | P0 | E001 | Same logical change and same status-condition data as HLR-1; shares the model serving views surface. |\n| HLR-3 (≤30s freshness, no manual reload) | P1 | E001 | Coupled to the same views; mechanism (polling vs. watch) is an implementation detail. |\n| HLR-4 (filter/sort list by status) | P2 | E001 | Bundled, not split: shares the deployed-models list UI surface and status data with the P0 work —