{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-614c098c-84c6-4d34-ba25-6a00e8b6a299","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4c5a131c22c5308","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9001-acbgcwq1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9001-E001.md","content":"# Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers deployment status visibility for KServe InferenceServices\ninside the RHOAI Dashboard. Data scientists will see at a glance whether each\ndeployed model is Ready, Progressing, or Failed, can drill into the underlying\ncondition messages and recent events for failed or progressing deployments,\nand see status stay current without a manual page reload. This removes the\nneed to leave the console and run `oc get inferenceservice` or read Kubernetes\nevents directly.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a deployment status (Ready, Progressing, Failed) for each deployed model\n  in the Dashboard model serving views, derived from the InferenceService CR\n  status conditions (e.g. Ready, PredictorReady) and related Kubernetes events.\n- Add a status detail view for a deployment showing the underlying condition\n  messages and recent events, reachable for failed or progressing deployments.\n- Keep the displayed status within 30 seconds of the actual InferenceService\n  state without requiring a manual page reload (refresh mechanism — e.g.\n  polling or watch — is an implementation decision for the Dashboard team).\n- Add filter and sort by status to the deployed models list.\n- KServe itself requires no code changes: the conditions and events are\n  already exposed on the InferenceService status. The serving team's\n  validation of that status-condition contract runs in parallel with this\n  work; coordinate on the condition-to-display-state mapping.\n- Out of scope per strategy: alerting/notifications on status transitions,\n  status history / timeline views, and ModelMesh deployments (KServe\n  InferenceService only).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a deployed KServe InferenceService, when a user opens the Dashboard\n  model serving views, then each deployed model shows a status of Ready,\n  Progressing, or Failed (HLR-1).\n- Given a failed or progressing deployment, when the user opens its status\n  detail view, then the underlying condition messages and recent events for\n  that deployment are shown (HLR-2).\n- Given a change in the actual InferenceService state, the displayed status\n  reflects it within 30 seconds, without a manual page reload (HLR-3).\n- Given the deployed models list, the user can filter it by status and sort\n  it by status (HLR-4).\n- The Ready/Progressing/Failed mapping is derived from the InferenceService\n  status conditions as documented in the KServe architecture context\n  (serving.kserve.io/v1beta1 conditions such as Ready and PredictorReady).\n- ModelMesh deployments are not covered by the status display (strategy\n  out-of-scope).\n- The Dashboard's existing build pipeline remains green with these changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): status shown per deployed model — this epic.\n- HLR-2 (P0): status detail view with conditions and events — this epic.\n- HLR-3 (P1): 30-second freshness without manual reload — this epic.\n- HLR-4 (P2): filter and sort by status — this epic (bundled: shares the\n  deployed-models list surface and status data with the P0 work).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30500,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5d445633276f153","agent_id":"a92205db70e46826d","session_id":"3b82bbf4-97d2-4391-a50a-11f44f5d64aa","uuid":"4a99f03d-c09e-411e-9908-f8ed48d1f879","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:16:18.381Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9001"}
