{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-6e2ccdd7-c40c-4e9f-8071-f5cee3179014","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-95158813d8684aef","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9001-acbgcwq1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9001-E002.md","content":"# Validate KServe InferenceService status-condition contract for Dashboard consumption\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers a validation of the existing KServe InferenceService\nstatus-condition and event contract that the Dashboard's deployment-status\nsurfacing relies on. KServe requires no code changes — the serving team\nconfirms that the conditions and events already exposed by the platform are\ncomplete, stable, and correctly interpretable for rendering Ready /\nProgressing / Failed states, and hands any gaps to the Dashboard effort.\nThe strategy marks this as non-blocking, so this validation runs in parallel\nwith the Dashboard implementation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Confirm the set of InferenceService status conditions (e.g. Ready,\n  PredictorReady) exposed via serving.kserve.io/v1beta1, and their semantics,\n  in both serverless and raw deployment modes.\n- Confirm that the conditions are sufficient to distinguish the Ready,\n  Progressing, and Failed display states the Dashboard must render, and\n  document the recommended condition-to-display-state mapping.\n- Confirm that relevant Kubernetes events (e.g. predictor failures, route\n  issues) are observable for failed and progressing InferenceServices and\n  carry useful messages for the status detail view.\n- Document findings — including any condition or event coverage gaps that\n  would prevent accurate status display — and hand them to the Dashboard\n  effort. Gaps are escalated as recommendations, not silently patched: no\n  KServe code changes are in scope for this epic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The InferenceService status conditions relevant to deployment health are\n  inventoried, with their semantics, across serverless and raw deployment\n  modes.\n- A documented mapping from condition states to the Ready / Progressing /\n  Failed display states is produced and handed off.\n- For a failing and for a progressing InferenceService, the observable\n  Kubernetes events are confirmed to include recent, informative messages\n  suitable for the status detail view.\n- Any gaps that would prevent accurate status display are documented with\n  remediation recommendations and communicated to the Dashboard team.\n- No KServe code changes are required as part of this validation (per the\n  strategy: KServe already exposes the needed conditions).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): status shown per deployed model — validates the data-source\n  contract behind this requirement (parallel, non-gating per strategy).\n- HLR-2 (P0): status detail view conditions and events — confirms the\n  condition messages and events the detail view will surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31385,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5d445633276f153","agent_id":"a92205db70e46826d","session_id":"3b82bbf4-97d2-4391-a50a-11f44f5d64aa","uuid":"cf5e8ea4-2131-4afd-94b4-5f4f6e5c645a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:16:34.453Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9001"}
