{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8821805ef45693b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9001-E002\n3\ttitle: Validate KServe InferenceService status-condition contract for Dashboard consumption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9001\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Validate KServe InferenceService status-condition contract for Dashboard consumption\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a validation of the existing KServe InferenceService\n34\tstatus-condition and event contract that the Dashboard's deployment-status\n35\tsurfacing relies on. KServe requires no code changes — the serving team\n36\tconfirms that the conditions and events already exposed by the platform are\n37\tcomplete, stable, and correctly interpretable for rendering Ready /\n38\tProgressing / Failed states, and hands any gaps to the Dashboard effort.\n39\tThe strategy marks this as non-blocking, so this validation runs in parallel\n40\twith the Dashboard implementation.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Confirm the set of InferenceService status conditions (e.g. Ready,\n45\t  PredictorReady) exposed via serving.kserve.io/v1beta1, and their semantics,\n46\t  in both serverless and raw deployment modes.\n47\t- Confirm that the conditions are sufficient to distinguish the Ready,\n48\t  Progressing, and Failed display states the Dashboard must render, and\n49\t  document the recommended condition-to-display-state mapping.\n50\t- Confirm that relevant Kubernetes events (e.g. predictor failures, route\n51\t  issues) are observable for failed and progressing InferenceServices and\n52\t  carry useful messages for the status detail view.\n53\t- Document findings — including any condition or event coverage gaps that\n54\t  would prevent accurate status display — and hand them to the Dashboard\n55\t  effort. Gaps are escalated as recommendations, not silently patched: no\n56\t  KServe code changes are in scope for this epic.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- The InferenceService status conditions relevant to deployment health are\n61\t  inventoried, with their semantics, across serverless and raw deployment\n62\t  modes.\n63\t- A documented mapping from condition states to the Ready / Progressing /\n64\t  Failed display states is produced and handed off.\n65\t- For a failing and for a progressing InferenceService, the observable\n66\t  Kubernetes events are confirmed to include recent, informative messages\n67\t  suitable for the status detail view.\n68\t- Any gaps that would prevent accurate status display are documented with\n69\t  remediation recommendations and communicated to the Dashboard team.\n70\t- No KServe code changes are required as part of this validation (per the\n71\t  strategy: KServe already exposes the needed conditions).\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-1 (P0): status shown per deployed model — validates the data-source\n76\t  contract behind this requirement (parallel, non-gating per strategy).\n77\t- HLR-2 (P0): status detail view conditions and events — confirms the\n78\t  condition messages and events the detail view will surface.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83656c89cfe7cac2","agent_id":"a3db62b666f7aad26","session_id":"3b82bbf4-97d2-4391-a50a-11f44f5d64aa","uuid":"ca641e46-8259-44fe-84f1-f831978bb571","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:23:13.490Z","tool_resul