ommon condition messages mean).\n52\t- Content authored in the Documentation component's docs repository following\n53\t  the Red Hat docs content process.\n54\t- Out of scope per strategy: alerting/notifications, status history, and\n55\t  ModelMesh deployments — the documentation covers KServe\n56\t  InferenceService-based deployments only.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Documentation explains each status value (Ready, Progressing, Failed) shown\n61\t  in the Dashboard model serving views (HLR-5).\n62\t- Documentation includes the first troubleshooting steps for Failed\n63\t  deployments, referencing the status detail view and its condition messages\n64\t  and events (HLR-5).\n65\t- Content is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior of the\n66\t  deployment-status feature and the validated KServe condition semantics\n67\t  before publication.\n68\t- Content follows the Red Hat docs content process for the Documentation\n69\t  component.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-5 (P2): product documentation for status values and Failed-deployment\n74\t  troubleshooting — this epic.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9502baf080c85957","agent_id":"a1a3ac3d2f4f3ae01","session_id":"3b82bbf4-97d2-4391-a50a-11f44f5d64aa","uuid":"464a674c-0b07-45cd-93b8-eabe62b5c2f6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:29:39.328Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-868b81e6e10a396d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9001 decomposition"}
