{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-908f41166fed9ec6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9001-E004\n3\ttitle: Filter and sort the deployed models list by deployment status\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9001\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Filter and sort the deployed models list by deployment status\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic adds filter and sort controls to the deployed models list in the\n34\tRHOAI Dashboard model serving views, keyed on the deployment status (Ready,\n35\tProgressing, Failed). It is a distinct, deferrable enhancement: users get\n36\tfull status visibility from the status-surfacing work without it, and this\n37\tepic can be planned, scheduled, or deferred independently because it is a\n38\tseparate P2 requirement in the strategy.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Add a status filter to the deployed models list so users can narrow the\n43\t  list to deployments in a selected status (Ready, Progressing, Failed).\n44\t- Add status-based sorting to the deployed models list.\n45\t- Build on the existing deployed-models list UI and the deployment status\n46\t  values rendered by the Dashboard's status-surfacing work; no new data\n47\t  sources, no backend changes, and no KServe changes — the underlying\n48\t  InferenceService conditions already exist in-platform.\n49\t- Runs alongside the status-surfacing work in the same repo and team; the\n50\t  shared list surface is a merge-coordination concern managed within the\n51\t  team, not a blocking dependency.\n52\t- Out of scope per strategy: alerting/notifications on status transitions,\n53\t  status history / timeline views, and ModelMesh deployments (KServe\n54\t  InferenceService only).\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Given the deployed models list, when the user applies a status filter, then\n59\t  only deployments with the selected status (Ready, Progressing, or Failed)\n60\t  are shown (HLR-4).\n61\t- Given the deployed models list, when the user sorts the list by status,\n62\t  then deployments are ordered by status according to the selected sort\n63\t  direction (HLR-4).\n64\t- The deployed models list remains fully usable when no filter is applied\n65\t  (no regression to the unfiltered list).\n66\t- The Dashboard's existing build pipeline remains green with these changes.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-4 (P2): filter and sort the deployed models list by status — this epic\n71\t  (split from the P0 status-surfacing work so the P2 capability can be\n72\t  planned and deferred independently).\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9502baf080c85957","agent_id":"a1a3ac3d2f4f3ae01","session_id":"3b82bbf4-97d2-4391-a50a-11f44f5d64aa","uuid":"8eecba38-80b6-4ed4-a1a0-d9d38611165e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:29:40.297Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-908f41166fed9ec6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9001 decomposition"}
