{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b74cb93714415d2d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Signals — RHAISTRAT-9001-E004\n2\t\n3\t**Epic**: Filter and sort the deployed models list by deployment status\n4\t**Type**: Implementation\n5\t\n6\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n7\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n8\t| change_specificity | 0 | The strategy states the capability functionally (filter and sort the deployed models list by status) with no field-level or component-level specifics for the Dashboard changes. |\n9\t| pattern_precedent | 1 | The Dashboard architecture context documents resource lists as the standard integration surface; list filter/sort controls are an established pattern in the same console and codebase. |\n10\t| adapter_pattern | 0 | Not an adapter/plugin-pattern change; N/A. |\n11\t| existing_foundation | 1 | Extends the existing deployed-models list in odh-dashboard and the status values surfaced there, rather than building greenfield. |\n12\t| open_questions | 1 | Strategy states no blocking open questions; filter/sort behavior is fully specified by HLR-4 with no approach-changing unknowns. |\n13\t| external_dependency | 1 | None — the InferenceService status conditions it filters on already exist in-platform; no upstream contribution or vendor coordination. |\n14\t| human_process_gates | 0 | No special approval steps stated; standard PR review only. A UI/UX review of the new controls is possible but unstated in the strategy. |\n15\t| repo_access | 1 | Target repo (opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard upstream) is public and clonable. |\n16\t| architecture_claims | 1 | The Dashboard architecture context corroborates that the model serving resource lists and their status views are the Dashboard's own surface — no unverifiable architecture claims. |\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9502baf080c85957","agent_id":"a1a3ac3d2f4f3ae01","session_id":"3b82bbf4-97d2-4391-a50a-11f44f5d64aa","uuid":"736075e